## Step 6 — Run /check-exercises

After writing, run `/check-exercises chN` to verify no unattested Greek vocabulary slipped into the exercises. Fix any real violations before committing.

---

## Content rules

- **All question and explanation text is in English.** Never put Greek in question or option text. Greek appears only in explanation fields when quoting the story directly, and only attested forms.
- **Story-grounded.** Every question must be directly answerable from the story. No theological inference, no outside knowledge.
- **No duplicate questions.** Vary the angle — plot facts, character motivations, sequence, contrast, dialogue.
- **Explanations are brief.** One sentence citing the story detail that makes the answer correct.
- **Part balance.** Do not weight one part heavily — aim for even coverage across A and B.
